-- title:
--   Lifting even rigidifications along square-zero thickenings
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`) and $N$ is a nonzero squarefree natural number (`hN`) divisible by neither $r$ (`hrN`) nor $\bar r$ (`hrbarN`).
--
--   **Base rings.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is complete for the $\pi$-adic filtration (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. The ring `Onr` is a characteristic-zero domain and an $\mathcal O$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism `Fr`, such that `Onr` is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of `Onr` satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally `vdet` is a homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) which, by `hvdet`, sends $g$ to $n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli schemes.** For rationals $a,b$, the hypothesis `hB` says that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $a>0$ or $b>0$ and that, for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$, the $v$-adic completion is a division algebra precisely when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ with structure map $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and the family of point maps `pt` (attaching to each ring $S$, each map $\operatorname{Spec} S \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and each fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over $S$ a point of $\mathcal X$ over that map) is a coarse moduli space: `h𝒳` bundles invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points of algebraically closed fields, and the universal property. The auxiliary level $n$ satisfies $3 \le n$ (`hn`), is prime to $r$ (`hrn`), to $\bar r$ (`hrbarn`) and to $N$ (`hnN`); $(M, f_M, \mathrm{ptF})$ is a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with full level $n$ (`hM`), and $(G,\rho,\chi)$ is a level-twist action on it (`hρ`: the automorphisms $\rho(h)$ lie over the base, they realise twisting of the level structure by $\chi(h) \in \Lambda$, and the labels $\chi$ are multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). The morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ lies over the base (`hp`), is invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and is compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, $(\mathcal Y_\ell, g_\ell, \mathrm{ptT}_\ell)$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (`h𝒴`), and $d_0,d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ lie over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) and induce on points, respectively, forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to the $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). The endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ lie over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) and induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion algebra and Hecke data.** For rationals $a_1,b_1$, `hdef` says $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $\bar r$. Here $\Lambda_1$ is maximal (`hΛ₁`), $R_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ (`hR₁`), with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); $n_1$ is a finite idele in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (`hn₁`) such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁`, the intersection of $R_1$ with its conjugate by $n_1$, is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and $v$ is the height-one prime containing $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\Gamma^t$ consists exactly of those units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37) (`hΓt`). For each prime $\ell \notin\{r,\bar r\}$ the hypothesis `hs` gives units $s_\ell$ and ideles $\mathrm{sf}_\ell$ such that the component of $\mathrm{sf}_\ell$ at each place not containing $r$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$, its component at the places containing $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $\mathrm{sf}_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and the reduced norm of $s_\ell$ is $\ell$; the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell$ are the intersections $\Gamma^t \cap s_\ell \Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). The unit $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`). Moreover $\Lambda$ contains all rational integers (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinate system for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`hcoord`: additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative in the twisted sense, injective, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity) with values in pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$.
--
--   **Uniformisation data on the special fibre.** Over $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension two for $A_0$, and the compatibility $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). Families $e, e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma^t$, with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees recorded by `deg`, satisfy: $e_\gamma, e'_\gamma$ form an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure (`hE1`); multiplicativity up to $r$-power scalars (`hE1mul`); for rational integral scalars $\gamma$, $e_\gamma$ is the corresponding scalar up to $r$-powers (`hE1sc`); conversely, an $e_\gamma$ which is a scalar up to $r$-powers forces $\gamma$ to be a scalar (`hE1'`); and, for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action and $\varpi$-endomorphisms of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$, there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image under $E_0$ is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ (`hE2`). The hypothesis `hE3` records that the action of $\Gamma^t$ on a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ is given by labels in $\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; `hE4` records that over any algebraically closed field any $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny pair of a pullback of $A_0$ comes, up to $r$-power scalars, from some $e_\gamma$. The order $R_2 \le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) has the property that $r$-power multiples of elements of $R_1$ lie in $R_2$ (`hR₂r`), and the family $\hat e$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`) is additive, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level (`hE5a`), is unital (`hE5b1`), multiplicative (`hE5b2`), agrees with the $\Lambda$-action on integers (`hE5b3`), satisfies $\hat e_{\bar x}\,\hat e_x =$ multiplication by the reduced norm (`hE5c`), is compatible with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$ (`hE5d`), and realises both $\Gamma^t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously through one conjugating matrix $g$ as in `hE2` (`hE5e`). Finally `P₀` is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$, and $A_{0w}$ together with $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ and $k_w$ exhibits $A_{0w}$ as an Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`, with `haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`) and $b_w$ as a level-preserving isogeny of degree $r^{k_w}$ back to $A_0$ (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), the composite $a_w \circ b_w$ being realised on formal coordinates by an element matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to $r$-powers and the same conjugation as for $\Gamma^t$ (`hJOINTw`).
--
--   **Drinfeld-side data.** There are a ring map $\iota$ from the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ into `Onr`, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), a moduli package `MD` over `Onr` which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and a family $\eta$ sending rigidified objects over $r$-nilpotent rings to points of `MD`; `hη` consists of three clauses: on admissible rigidified objects over Noetherian rings, $\eta$ identifies two of them exactly when they are isomorphic; $\eta$ commutes with base change along ring maps; and every point of `MD` comes from admissible rigidified objects after passing to a Zariski cover by localisations. The ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action and $\varpi$-endomorphisms of $\Phi$ to $M_2(K_0)$ is injective, and for some exponent $m$ the set $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ lies in its image while $r^{m}$ times its image lies in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). The family `eD` compares, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, the objects of the functor `ModuliPackage.G 𝒪 MD` at $B$ with pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (a point of the formal upper half plane $\hat\Omega$ over $\mathcal O$ with $K_0$ and $\pi$); it is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), has first component the structural map $\psi$ (`hfstD`), translates the action of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), translates $\pi$-translation into a Frobenius twist of the first leg leaving the datum unchanged (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`). The map $\kappa$ is compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the pushforward of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **The comparison map.** The family $\Xi$ assigns to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and each rigidified fake elliptic curve over $B$ relative to $A_0$ a point of `MD` over $\mathcal O$. Its properties are: over connected $B$ its $\psi$-leg is a Frobenius twist $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ of $\psi$ (`hΞleg`); it is natural under pullback of rigidified curves (`hΞnat`); it is unchanged when two rigidified curves are related by an isomorphism together with comparison data on the reductions and on the auxiliary pullbacks of $A_0$, matching the isogenies up to $r$-power scalars (`hΞiso`); and it is computed explicitly (`hΞdef`): whenever the underlying curve is a formal module via `coord` with data $X,\theta$, there exist $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, related to the given rigidification by `IsRigTransport` through $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$, such that $\Xi$ equals the point with $\psi$-leg $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and moduli component $\eta(t)$. Finally $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and `heqΓ`, `heqW` state that over connected $B$ a translation of a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ (respectively a passage to an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, with $\bar r$ invertible in $B$ and comparison data involving $a_w \circ b_w$) is implemented on the $\Xi$-images by the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$, respectively $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$, for some integer $c$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\psi^{\flat} := \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ for the Frobenius twist of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi$ by minus the valuation of $\det g_0$. Under all the above hypotheses the following holds. Let $B$ and $B_0$ be Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, and let $p : B \to B_0$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map whose kernel has square zero, in the form: $st = 0$ whenever $p(s) = p(t) = 0$. Let $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve with level $N$ over $B$, let $E_0$ be one over $B_0$, and let $g : E_0.A \to E.A$ exhibit $E_0$ as the pullback of $E$ along $p$ (`hg`). Let $\varrho_0$ be a rigidification of $E_0$ relative to $A_0$ over $(p \circ \psi)^{\flat}$ — that is, a reduction of $E_0$ modulo $\pi$ with its comparison map, a pullback of $A_0$ along the residue leg of $(p\circ\psi)^{\flat}$, and a level-preserving isogeny pair of degree a power of $r$ between the two — and assume that the $\psi$-leg of $\Xi$ at $\langle E_0, \varrho_0\rangle$ is exactly $(p\circ\psi)^{\flat}$. Then there exist a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ over $\psi^{\flat}$ and a rigidification $\varrho_0'$ of $E_0$ relative to $A_0$ over $(p\circ\psi)^{\flat}$ such that:
--
--   (i) $\varrho_0'$ is the pullback of $\varrho$ along $p$ via $g$, i.e. there are comparison maps on the reductions and on the pullbacks of $A_0$ which are themselves pullbacks along the induced map of $\pi$-reductions, commute with the maps to $E$ and to $A_0$, have equal isogeny degrees and make the isogeny squares commute;
--
--   (ii) the $\psi$-leg of $\Xi$ at $\langle E, \varrho\rangle$ is exactly $\psi^{\flat}$;
--
--   (iii) for every Deligne datum $P_0'$ over $B_0$, the pair $((p\circ\psi), P_0')$ is obtained from `eD` applied to $\Xi\langle E_0,\varrho_0\rangle$ by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action if and only if it is so obtained from `eD` applied to $\Xi\langle E_0,\varrho_0'\rangle$; that is, $\varrho_0$ and $\varrho_0'$ have the same image point in the formal upper half plane, untwisted by $g_0$.
--
--   This is the infinitesimal lifting step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: a rigidification of a fake elliptic curve over a quotient by a square-zero ideal lifts to the thickening, the lift remaining compatible with the normalisation that pins down its Frobenius leg, and agreeing with the given rigidification at the level of the associated point of the formal upper half plane rather than on the nose, since $r$-power scalars act freely. It is used where the lift is shown to be unique up to this correspondence, and in the construction of the fine moduli family with extra level structure along the Hecke tower.
